1
00:01:53,330 --> 00:01:55,930
The  Bells

2
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:12,760
“八爪蜘蛛”

3
00:02:26,390 --> 00:02:27,310
Come in.

4
00:02:31,310 --> 00:02:32,430
And?

5
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:35,770
Nothing?

6
00:02:35,850 --> 00:02:37,470
She won't eat.

7
00:02:42,350 --> 00:02:44,560
We'll try again at supper.

8
00:02:46,810 --> 00:02:48,470
I think they're watching me.

9
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:53,390
- Who? - Her soldiers.

10
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:57,430
Of course they are. That's their job.

11
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:09,390
What have I told you, Martha?

12
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:13,930
The greater the risk, the greater the reward.

13
00:03:15,270 --> 00:03:18,140
Go on. They'll be missing you in the kitchen.

14
00:03:30,090 --> 00:03:33,470
“小恶魔” 丹妮莉丝的女王之手

15
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,310
The Northern armies?

16
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:44,890
Just crossed the Trident.

17
00:03:44,970 --> 00:03:47,850
They'll be at the walls of King's Landing in two days.

18
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:50,520
How is she?

19
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:53,220
She hasn't seen anyone since we returned.

20
00:03:53,310 --> 00:03:56,640
Hasn't left her chambers, hasn't accepted any food.

21
00:03:57,810 --> 00:03:59,560
She shouldn't be alone.

22
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:02,720
You're worried for her. I admire your empathy.

23
00:04:02,810 --> 00:04:04,680
Aren't you worried for her?

24
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:06,890
I'm worried for all of us.

25
00:04:06,970 --> 00:04:09,140
They say every time a Targaryen is born,

26
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:12,430
the gods toss a coin and the world holds its breath.

27
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:15,270
We're not much for riddles where I'm from.

28
00:04:15,350 --> 00:04:18,180
We both know what she's about to do.

29
00:04:21,390 --> 00:04:24,560
伊耿·坦格利安 铁王座法理继承人

30
00:04:24,060 --> 00:04:26,410
That's her decision to make. She is our queen.

31
00:04:26,410 --> 00:04:30,390
Men decide where power resides, whether or not they know it.

32
00:04:32,930 --> 00:04:34,720
What do you want?

33
00:04:34,810 --> 00:04:36,560
All I've ever wanted.

34
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:39,560
The right ruler on the Iron Throne.

35
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:43,930
I still don't know how her coin has landed.

36
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:47,350
But I'm quite certain about yours.

37
00:04:55,390 --> 00:04:57,310
I don't want it.

38
00:04:57,390 --> 00:04:58,720
I never have.

39
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:04,890
I have known more kings and queens than any man living.

40
00:05:04,970 --> 00:05:06,640
I've heard what they say to crowds,

41
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,560
and seen what they do in the shadows.

42
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:12,020
I have furthered their designs, however horrible.

43
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:14,810
But what I tell you now is true:

44
00:05:14,890 --> 00:05:18,100
You will rule wisely and well, while she--

45
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:19,970
She...

46
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:21,140
is my queen.

47
00:05:42,970 --> 00:05:44,430
Your Grace?

48
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:12,100
There's something you need to know.

49
00:06:12,380 --> 00:06:15,260
“风暴降生”“龙之母”

50
00:06:13,390 --> 00:06:15,640
Someone has betrayed me.

51
00:06:21,810 --> 00:06:23,180
Yes.

52
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:28,930
Jon Snow.

53
00:06:34,810 --> 00:06:35,770
Varys.

54
00:06:37,970 --> 00:06:40,100
He knows the truth about Jon.

55
00:06:41,390 --> 00:06:42,930
He does.

56
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:50,020
Because you told him.

57
00:06:52,310 --> 00:06:54,060
You learned from Sansa.

58
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:56,680
And she learned from Jon,

59
00:06:56,770 --> 00:06:59,350
though I begged him not to tell her.

60
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:02,560
As I said...

61
00:07:03,310 --> 00:07:04,390
he betrayed me.

62
00:07:04,470 --> 00:07:06,310
I'm glad Sansa told me.

63
00:07:06,390 --> 00:07:07,930
I am your Hand.

64
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:10,520
I need to be aware of any threats you're facing.

65
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:13,310
And Varys?

66
00:07:13,390 --> 00:07:16,520
Your Master of Whisperers needs to be aware too.

67
00:07:17,350 --> 00:07:19,770
You spoke to him first.

68
00:07:19,850 --> 00:07:21,100
Without coming to me.

69
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:23,640
Without asking my permission.

70
00:07:25,270 --> 00:07:27,890
It was a mistake.

71
00:07:29,890 --> 00:07:32,680
Why do you think Sansa told you?

72
00:07:32,770 --> 00:07:34,520
What do you think she hoped to gain?

73
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:38,180
- She trusts me. - Yes, she trusts you.

74
00:07:39,310 --> 00:07:43,390
She trusted you to spread secrets

75
00:07:43,470 --> 00:07:46,560
that could destroy your own queen.

76
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:50,850
And you did not let her down.

77
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:58,060
If I have failed you, my queen, forgive me.

78
00:07:59,930 --> 00:08:02,220
Our intentions were good.

79
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:07,220
We wanted what you want. A better world, all of us.

80
00:08:08,470 --> 00:08:11,310
Varys as much as anyone.

81
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:22,140
But it doesn't matter now.

82
00:08:24,310 --> 00:08:25,270
No.

83
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:28,270
It doesn't matter now.

84
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:27,530
无垢者指挥官

85
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:30,680
It was me.

86
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:37,680
I hope I deserve this.

87
00:10:37,770 --> 00:10:39,430
Truly, I do.

88
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:41,600
I hope I'm wrong.

89
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:50,220
Goodbye, old friend.

90
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:32,810
Lord Varys.

91
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:36,720
I, Daenerys of House Targaryen,

92
00:11:36,810 --> 00:11:38,640
First of My Name,

93
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:41,970
Breaker of Chains and Mother of Dragons...

94
00:11:43,810 --> 00:11:45,850
sentence you to die.

95
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:47,550
丹妮莉丝的黑龙

96
00:11:56,350 --> 00:11:57,470
Dracarys.

97
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:50,190
This was all she brought with her

98
00:12:50,190 --> 00:12:52,220
when we crossed the Narrow Sea.

99
00:12:53,310 --> 00:12:55,350
Her only possession.

100
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:13,680
What did I say would happen if you told your sister?

101
00:14:13,770 --> 00:14:17,060
I don't want it, and that's what I told him.

102
00:14:18,350 --> 00:14:20,560
She betrayed your trust.

103
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:22,390
She killed Varys as much as I did.

104
00:14:24,020 --> 00:14:26,470
This was a victory for her.

105
00:14:27,970 --> 00:14:29,380
Now she knows what happens

106
00:14:29,380 --> 00:14:31,180
when people hear the truth about you.

107
00:14:33,810 --> 00:14:37,810
Far more people in Westeros love you than love me.

108
00:14:40,310 --> 00:14:42,680
I don't have love here.

109
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:46,180
I only have fear.

110
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:50,970
I love you.

111
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:56,310
And you will always be my queen.

112
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:05,140
Is that all I am to you?

113
00:15:06,890 --> 00:15:08,850
Your queen?

114
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:47,680
All right, then.

115
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:56,890
Let it be fear.

116
00:16:00,890 --> 00:16:04,140
The people who live there, they're not your enemies.

117
00:16:04,430 --> 00:16:07,340
They're innocents, like the ones you liberated in Meereen.

118
00:16:07,350 --> 00:16:09,320
In Meereen, the slaves turned on the masters

119
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:12,140
and liberated the city themselves the moment I arrived.

120
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:13,430
They're afraid.

121
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:14,840
Anyone who resists Cersei

122
00:16:14,850 --> 00:16:16,970
will see his family butchered.

123
00:16:17,060 --> 00:16:19,270
You can't expect them to be heroes.

124
00:16:19,350 --> 00:16:21,470
- They're hostages. - They are.

125
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:24,890
In a tyrant's grip. Whose fault is that? Mine?

126
00:16:24,970 --> 00:16:27,600
What does it matter whose fault it is?

127
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:30,560
Thousands of children will die if the city burns.

128
00:16:30,640 --> 00:16:31,890
Your sister knows how to use

129
00:16:31,970 --> 00:16:34,020
her enemies' weaknesses against them.

130
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:36,520
That's what she thinks our mercy is:

131
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,770
weakness.

132
00:16:37,850 --> 00:16:39,930
- I beg you, my queen - But she's wrong.

133
00:16:40,810 --> 00:16:42,600
Mercy is our strength.

134
00:16:43,850 --> 00:16:46,220
Our mercy towards future generations

135
00:16:46,310 --> 00:16:48,890
who will never again be held hostage by a tyrant.

136
00:16:54,850 --> 00:16:56,470
Ready the Unsullied.

137
00:16:56,560 --> 00:16:58,380
Tonight you sail for King's Landing

138
00:16:58,380 --> 00:17:00,180
- to join the Northern armies. - Cersei's followers

139
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:02,180
will abandon her if they know the war is lost.

140
00:17:02,180 --> 00:17:03,640
Give them that chance.

141
00:17:04,590 --> 00:17:06,190
If the city surrenders,

142
00:17:06,190 --> 00:17:07,800
they will ring the bells and raise the gates.

143
00:17:07,810 --> 00:17:11,470
Please, if you hear them ringing the bells, call off the attack.

144
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:21,640
Wait for me outside the city.

145
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:24,430
You'll know when it's time.

146
00:17:53,970 --> 00:17:57,850
Your brother was stopped trying to get past our lines.

147
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:05,680
It seems he hasn't abandoned your sister after all.

148
00:18:11,390 --> 00:18:13,020
The next time you fail me...

149
00:18:14,390 --> 00:18:16,850
will be the last time you fail me.

150
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:35,640
Let them pass.

151
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:48,640
Through the gate.

152
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:34,560
The rearguard should be here by daybreak.

153
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:37,100
She wants to attack now.

154
00:19:35,180 --> 00:19:38,180
“洋葱骑士”

155
00:19:38,310 --> 00:19:39,770
Daybreak at the earliest.

156
00:19:46,890 --> 00:19:48,100
Davos.

157
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:52,970
I need to ask you a favor.

158
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:57,600
You're the greatest smuggler alive, aren't you?

159
00:19:59,140 --> 00:20:02,520
I'm not gonna like this favor, am I?

160
00:20:13,060 --> 00:20:15,930
Ay up. Where you going?

161
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:20,680
“猎狗”

162
00:20:17,350 --> 00:20:19,350
I'm Arya Stark.

163
00:20:19,430 --> 00:20:21,970
I'm going to kill Queen Cersei.

164
00:20:26,470 --> 00:20:27,470
Think about it.

165
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:30,180
She kills Cersei, the war's over.

166
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:33,640
There won't be a siege.You might not even die tomorrow.

167
00:20:36,930 --> 00:20:38,770
I need to go talk to my captain.

168
00:20:38,850 --> 00:20:40,850
Go ahead, talk to him.

169
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:45,310
Where's he going?

170
00:21:15,430 --> 00:21:17,020
We speak the common tongue.

171
00:21:18,020 --> 00:21:19,930
Ah. Good.

172
00:21:20,020 --> 00:21:21,770
I want to be alone with the prisoner.

173
00:21:21,850 --> 00:21:24,020
Get some rest. Tomorrow will be a long day.

174
00:21:24,100 --> 00:21:26,470
We have orders to guard the prisoner.

175
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:28,350
Ordered by whom? The queen herself?

176
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:31,830
- No. - Well, in that case,

177
00:21:31,830 --> 00:21:34,560
as Hand of the Queen, I outrank whomever gave your order.

178
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:36,180
Probably by quite a lot.

179
00:21:53,110 --> 00:21:56,110
“弑君者”

180
00:21:59,890 --> 00:22:01,890
How did they find you?

181
00:22:10,060 --> 00:22:12,470
Did you consider taking it off?

182
00:22:13,930 --> 00:22:17,390
Cersei once called me "the stupidest Lannister."

183
00:22:18,890 --> 00:22:22,140
And you're going back to her, to die with her.

184
00:22:23,310 --> 00:22:24,930
You've underestimated her before.

185
00:22:24,940 --> 00:22:26,490
She's going to die.

186
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:29,060
Unless you can convince her

187
00:22:29,060 --> 00:22:30,680
to change her course of action.

188
00:22:30,770 --> 00:22:32,770
Difficult to do from here.

189
00:22:38,390 --> 00:22:41,520
When have I ever been able to convince Cersei of anything?

190
00:22:41,600 --> 00:22:43,180
Try.

191
00:22:43,270 --> 00:22:45,290
If not for yourself, if not for her,

192
00:22:45,620 --> 00:22:48,180
then for every one of the million people in that city,

193
00:22:48,180 --> 00:22:49,660
innocent or otherwise.

194
00:22:49,660 --> 00:22:52,560
To be honest, I never really cared much for them.

195
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:54,470
Innocent or otherwise.

196
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:57,770
You do care for one innocent.

197
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:00,180
I know you do.

198
00:23:00,270 --> 00:23:02,020
And so does Cersei.

199
00:23:03,310 --> 00:23:05,020
She has a reason now.

200
00:23:06,470 --> 00:23:10,220
The child is the reason she'll never give an inch.

201
00:23:10,310 --> 00:23:12,100
All the worst things she's ever done,

202
00:23:12,180 --> 00:23:14,560
she's done for her children.

203
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:16,810
It's not impossible that she'll win.

204
00:23:16,890 --> 00:23:18,100
She won't.

205
00:23:18,180 --> 00:23:20,190
Her enemy's forces have been depleted,

206
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:21,750
as she said they would be.

207
00:23:21,750 --> 00:23:23,850
Two of the three dragons are dead.

208
00:23:23,930 --> 00:23:26,780
- She's evened the odds. - The city will fall tomorrow.

209
00:23:26,790 --> 00:23:28,620
She has the Lannister army, she has the Golden Company--

210
00:23:28,630 --> 00:23:30,630
I defended the city last time it was attacked.

211
00:23:30,630 --> 00:23:32,810
I know it better than anyone. It will fall tomorrow.

212
00:23:32,810 --> 00:23:35,400
Then I suppose I'll die tomorrow, if not before.

213
00:23:35,410 --> 00:23:37,020
Why?

214
00:23:43,220 --> 00:23:44,720
Escape.

215
00:23:44,810 --> 00:23:46,810
The two of you, together.

216
00:23:46,890 --> 00:23:48,460
Remember where we met,

217
00:23:48,490 --> 00:23:50,100
where they keep the dragon skulls,

218
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:51,280
beneath the Red Keep?

219
00:23:52,680 --> 00:23:53,970
Take her down there.

220
00:23:54,060 --> 00:23:55,830
Keep following the stairways down,

221
00:23:55,830 --> 00:23:57,150
down as far as they'll go.

222
00:23:57,160 --> 00:23:59,600
You'll come out onto a beach at the foot of the keep.

223
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:01,640
A dinghy will be waiting for you.

224
00:24:02,850 --> 00:24:04,220
Sail out of the bay.

225
00:24:04,310 --> 00:24:07,020
If the winds are kind, you'll make it to Pentos.

226
00:24:08,180 --> 00:24:10,600
Start a new life.

227
00:24:13,930 --> 00:24:17,270
Sail right past the Iron Fleet and into a new life?

228
00:24:17,350 --> 00:24:20,020
Sounds a lot less likely than Cersei winning this war--

229
00:24:20,100 --> 00:24:22,720
There won't be an Iron Fleet for much longer.

230
00:24:23,930 --> 00:24:25,180
Do it.

231
00:24:25,270 --> 00:24:28,390
If you don't, you'll never see Cersei again.

232
00:24:34,270 --> 00:24:36,060
Swear to me.

233
00:24:39,350 --> 00:24:41,270
You have my word.

234
00:24:45,890 --> 00:24:47,310
If it works,

235
00:24:47,390 --> 00:24:49,360
give the order to ring all the bells

236
00:24:49,360 --> 00:24:51,430
in King's Landing and open the gates.

237
00:24:51,430 --> 00:24:53,820
That will be our signal that the city has surrendered.

238
00:24:53,830 --> 00:24:55,310
I'll try.

239
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:59,100
I never thought I'd get to repay the favor.

240
00:24:59,180 --> 00:25:02,100
Remember, ring the bells and open the gates.

241
00:25:02,100 --> 00:25:04,420
Your queen will execute you for this.

242
00:25:04,430 --> 00:25:06,280
If Daenerys can make it to the throne

243
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:08,430
without wading through a river of blood,

244
00:25:08,520 --> 00:25:09,670
maybe she'll show mercy

245
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:11,930
to the person who made that possible.

246
00:25:17,680 --> 00:25:20,430
Tens of thousands of innocent lives...

247
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:24,930
one not particularly innocent dwarf...

248
00:25:26,350 --> 00:25:28,930
it seems like a fair trade.

249
00:25:35,470 --> 00:25:37,470
If it weren't for you,

250
00:25:37,560 --> 00:25:39,720
I never would've survived my childhood.

251
00:25:41,850 --> 00:25:43,680
You would have.

252
00:25:51,310 --> 00:25:52,850
You were the only one

253
00:25:54,060 --> 00:25:56,970
who didn't treat me like a monster.

254
00:25:59,560 --> 00:26:01,810
You were all I had.

255
00:27:07,050 --> 00:27:10,180
铁群岛之王

256
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:15,100
Eyes on the horizon!

257
00:27:16,390 --> 00:27:18,390
Load the scorpion!

258
00:27:31,640 --> 00:27:33,060
Archers, close up!

259
00:27:33,140 --> 00:27:34,520
Come on!

260
00:27:34,600 --> 00:27:36,600
Up to the espringal!

261
00:27:36,680 --> 00:27:38,890
To the back of it!

262
00:27:50,850 --> 00:27:52,560
Archers, line up!

263
00:28:00,600 --> 00:28:02,100
This way! Come on!

264
00:28:02,180 --> 00:28:03,770
Clear the streets now!

265
00:28:03,850 --> 00:28:06,100
- No! - In, now.

266
00:28:06,180 --> 00:28:08,850
- And you, come on. - Inside, now!

267
00:28:08,930 --> 00:28:10,350
Quickly.

268
00:28:10,430 --> 00:28:11,520
Yes. Follow down there.

269
00:28:11,600 --> 00:28:13,390
They're here. Get to the Red Keep.

270
00:28:15,100 --> 00:28:17,060
- My son! - Get inside!

271
00:28:21,390 --> 00:28:23,310
Just ahead of you, I can see it!

272
00:28:23,390 --> 00:28:24,720
All right, move it!

273
00:28:24,810 --> 00:28:26,640
- Come on! - Keep moving!

274
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:28,390
- Keep going! - Keep moving!

275
00:28:28,470 --> 00:28:30,220
- Quickly! - All the way!

276
00:28:30,310 --> 00:28:32,220
- Come on! - Come on!

277
00:28:32,310 --> 00:28:34,430
Hold your mother's hand!

278
00:28:47,180 --> 00:28:51,100
Make way for the Golden Company!

279
00:29:00,140 --> 00:29:01,390
Close the gate!

280
00:29:33,100 --> 00:29:36,320
黄金团团长

281
00:30:05,850 --> 00:30:08,890
If you hear the bells ring, they've surrendered.

282
00:30:08,970 --> 00:30:10,890
Call off your men.

283
00:30:23,220 --> 00:30:25,470
Move along now, lads.

284
00:30:42,510 --> 00:30:45,350
铁王座上的女王

285
00:30:54,220 --> 00:30:56,810
- That's it. - Go on, move it.

286
00:31:00,060 --> 00:31:03,310
Come on, move, move. Faster, faster. Come on, move it.

287
00:31:03,390 --> 00:31:05,220
- Keep going. - Keep moving.

288
00:31:09,060 --> 00:31:11,430
- Move. - Stay with him.

289
00:31:12,640 --> 00:31:14,220
- Hold on. - Hold my hand.

290
00:31:14,310 --> 00:31:15,520
Get behind there.

291
00:31:15,600 --> 00:31:17,720
Close the gate!

292
00:31:17,810 --> 00:31:19,430
No more through.

293
00:31:22,310 --> 00:31:24,850
- No. - No. Mommy.

294
00:31:24,930 --> 00:31:27,720
- Vicky! Please! - No, please, sir!

295
00:31:27,810 --> 00:31:30,180
- Open the gate! - Close the gate!

296
00:31:30,270 --> 00:31:32,100
- Open it! - Open the gate!

297
00:31:32,180 --> 00:31:35,970
- Get back. - Look, try that one. Go. Go.

298
00:31:41,810 --> 00:31:43,890
The gates are locked now!

299
00:31:43,970 --> 00:31:45,310
Open!

300
00:31:45,390 --> 00:31:47,560
- Get back! - Open the gate!

301
00:31:47,640 --> 00:31:50,350
Soldier! Soldier!

302
00:31:50,430 --> 00:31:53,430
- Please open the gate! - Go back to your homes!

303
00:31:53,520 --> 00:31:55,020
Stay back! It's closed!

304
00:31:55,100 --> 00:31:56,520
Soldier!

305
00:31:58,020 --> 00:31:59,310
Move away! Stop!

306
00:31:59,390 --> 00:32:02,060
Let us in!

307
00:32:04,520 --> 00:32:06,680
We're not leaving!

308
00:33:15,140 --> 00:33:16,430
Turn!

309
00:33:35,600 --> 00:33:39,430
Turn it around!

310
00:33:42,270 --> 00:33:44,270
Get back! Back!

311
00:33:48,850 --> 00:33:50,220
Fire!

312
00:34:10,470 --> 00:34:12,770
I can see her!

313
00:34:12,850 --> 00:34:14,020
Ready!

314
00:34:14,100 --> 00:34:15,430
Move!

315
00:34:17,640 --> 00:34:18,770
Fire!

316
00:34:22,970 --> 00:34:24,930
- Reload! - Reload!

317
00:34:25,020 --> 00:34:26,680
Faster!

318
00:34:26,770 --> 00:34:27,970
Hurry!

319
00:34:37,270 --> 00:34:38,310
Fire!

320
00:37:59,720 --> 00:38:01,390
Go!

321
00:38:04,640 --> 00:38:06,560
Run!

322
00:38:18,930 --> 00:38:20,020
Your Grace.

323
00:38:21,020 --> 00:38:23,350
All we need is one good shot.

324
00:38:23,430 --> 00:38:27,220
The scorpions have all been destroyed, Your Grace.

325
00:38:24,360 --> 00:38:27,350
被剥夺项链的学士 瑟曦的女王之手

326
00:38:24,360 --> 00:38:27,350
“魔山”

327
00:38:29,060 --> 00:38:31,850
The Iron Fleet hold Blackwater Bay.

328
00:38:33,270 --> 00:38:35,140
Euron killed one of her dragons.

329
00:38:35,220 --> 00:38:36,640
He can kill another.

330
00:38:36,720 --> 00:38:39,890
Your Grace, the Iron Fleet is burning.

331
00:38:39,970 --> 00:38:42,140
The gates have been breached.

332
00:38:42,220 --> 00:38:43,990
The Golden Company--

333
00:38:43,990 --> 00:38:47,220
Our men will fight harder than sellswords ever could.

334
00:38:48,700 --> 00:38:51,190
They will defend their queen to the last man.

335
00:38:51,200 --> 00:38:54,270
- Yes, Your Grace. - The Red Keep has never fallen.

336
00:38:54,350 --> 00:38:56,310
It won't fall today.

337
00:39:25,220 --> 00:39:26,810
No, no, no!

338
00:39:30,020 --> 00:39:31,970
Move, move!

339
00:40:33,600 --> 00:40:35,020
Run.

340
00:40:35,100 --> 00:40:36,600
Run!

341
00:40:36,680 --> 00:40:37,850
Come on!

342
00:41:29,470 --> 00:41:32,930
- Ring the bells! - Ring the bells!

343
00:41:33,810 --> 00:41:35,140
The bells!

344
00:41:35,220 --> 00:41:38,310
- Ring the bells! - Ring the bells!

345
00:41:38,390 --> 00:41:40,520
Ring the bloody bells!

346
00:41:40,600 --> 00:41:43,270
- Ring the bells! - Ring the bells!

347
00:41:44,680 --> 00:41:46,560
Tell the queen to ring the bells.

348
00:41:46,640 --> 00:41:49,060
Ring the bells! Ring the bell!

349
00:41:57,270 --> 00:41:58,600
This way.

350
00:42:03,850 --> 00:42:05,310
Ring the bell!

351
00:42:06,310 --> 00:42:08,020
Ring the bell!

352
00:42:08,100 --> 00:42:09,430
Ring them!

353
00:42:12,720 --> 00:42:14,810
Ring the bells!

354
00:42:18,180 --> 00:42:20,680
Ring the bells!

355
00:42:20,770 --> 00:42:24,220
- Ring the bells! - Help us!

356
00:42:24,310 --> 00:42:25,600
In the name of the--

357
00:42:27,140 --> 00:42:29,100
Queen! We're surrounded!

358
00:42:36,310 --> 00:42:38,810
- Ring the bells! - Now! Come on!

359
00:42:45,930 --> 00:42:46,970
Hurry up!

360
00:42:56,810 --> 00:42:58,060
Ring the bells!

361
00:45:22,970 --> 00:45:24,140
No!

362
00:45:24,220 --> 00:45:25,350
Get back!

363
00:45:25,430 --> 00:45:26,470
Get back!

364
00:45:27,970 --> 00:45:30,020
Stay! Stay!

365
00:46:52,810 --> 00:46:54,560
No, no, no, no, no.

366
00:47:03,640 --> 00:47:05,770
Quickly. Quickly.

367
00:47:07,810 --> 00:47:09,270
Stop!

368
00:47:32,600 --> 00:47:35,430
- Get off me! Get off, bitch! - No, get off! Help! Help!

369
00:47:36,470 --> 00:47:37,560
No!

370
00:48:07,560 --> 00:48:08,770
Go!

371
00:48:10,140 --> 00:48:11,270
Go!

372
00:48:48,930 --> 00:48:50,810
Find somewhere to hide.

373
00:49:15,310 --> 00:49:16,560
My God!

374
00:49:35,520 --> 00:49:37,390
The Kingslayer.

375
00:49:39,890 --> 00:49:42,810
We need to get the queen out of King's Landing.

376
00:49:42,890 --> 00:49:44,520
Listen.

377
00:49:44,600 --> 00:49:48,060
That's the sound of a city dying.

378
00:49:50,020 --> 00:49:51,180
It's over.

379
00:49:51,270 --> 00:49:53,100
Well, maybe for you.

380
00:49:54,390 --> 00:49:57,430
If you kill another king before you die...

381
00:49:58,640 --> 00:50:00,390
they'll sing about you forever.

382
00:50:01,430 --> 00:50:03,100
You're no king.

383
00:50:03,180 --> 00:50:04,600
Oh, but I am.

384
00:50:06,390 --> 00:50:08,100
And I fucked the queen.

385
00:50:11,770 --> 00:50:12,810
If I win...

386
00:50:14,060 --> 00:50:15,670
I'll bring your head to Cersei

387
00:50:15,670 --> 00:50:18,540
so you can kiss her one last time.

388
00:52:02,350 --> 00:52:04,790
Your Grace, it isn't safe here any longer.

389
00:52:04,800 --> 00:52:07,000
The Red Keep is the safest place in the city.

390
00:52:07,000 --> 00:52:10,200
The Unsullied have breached the gates of the Red Keep.

391
00:52:18,640 --> 00:52:22,020
Maegor's Holdfast would be a better place

392
00:52:22,030 --> 00:52:23,510
to wait out the storm.

393
00:53:00,640 --> 00:53:02,600
You fought well...

394
00:53:03,600 --> 00:53:04,970
for a cripple.

395
00:53:49,360 --> 00:53:51,010
Another king for you.

396
00:54:05,890 --> 00:54:07,220
But I got you!

397
00:54:10,140 --> 00:54:11,380
I got you!

398
00:54:17,680 --> 00:54:20,520
I'm the man who killed Jaime Lannister.

399
00:54:44,970 --> 00:54:46,060
Go home, girl.

400
00:54:47,180 --> 00:54:48,770
The fire will get her,

401
00:54:48,850 --> 00:54:50,600
or one of the Dothraki.

402
00:54:51,850 --> 00:54:54,560
Or maybe that dragon will eat her.

403
00:54:54,640 --> 00:54:56,640
It doesn't matter. She's dead.

404
00:54:56,720 --> 00:54:59,520
And you'll be dead too if you don't get out of here.

405
00:55:00,560 --> 00:55:01,930
I'm going to kill her.

406
00:55:03,470 --> 00:55:06,310
You think you wanted revenge a long time?

407
00:55:06,390 --> 00:55:08,460
I've been after it all my life.

408
00:55:08,470 --> 00:55:10,270
It's all I care about.

409
00:55:10,350 --> 00:55:12,720
And look at me. Look at me!

410
00:55:14,720 --> 00:55:17,060
You wanna be like me?

411
00:55:23,890 --> 00:55:28,100
You come with me, you die here.

412
00:55:41,470 --> 00:55:42,890
Sandor.

413
00:55:49,770 --> 00:55:51,430
Thank you.

414
00:56:53,720 --> 00:56:55,470
Your Grace.

415
00:57:12,180 --> 00:57:14,520
Hello, big brother.

416
00:57:20,430 --> 00:57:23,020
Ser Gregor, stay by my side.

417
00:57:32,930 --> 00:57:34,540
Ser Gregor, I command you.

418
00:57:34,550 --> 00:57:36,080
Obey your queen, Ser Gregor.

419
00:58:33,270 --> 00:58:35,970
Yeah, that's you.

420
00:58:38,220 --> 00:58:40,100
That's what you've always been.

421
01:00:14,890 --> 01:00:16,180
You're hurt.

422
01:00:18,060 --> 01:00:19,390
It doesn't matter.

423
01:00:27,060 --> 01:00:28,890
You're bleeding.

424
01:02:11,430 --> 01:02:13,390
Alanna!

425
01:02:13,470 --> 01:02:15,890
Alanna! Have you seen my wife?

426
01:02:17,850 --> 01:02:19,470
Have you seen my wife?

427
01:02:35,390 --> 01:02:36,850
Out of the way!

428
01:03:04,430 --> 01:03:05,720
No!

429
01:03:36,600 --> 01:03:38,060
Oh.

430
01:04:07,350 --> 01:04:08,850
Take my hand.

431
01:04:08,930 --> 01:04:10,850
Take my hand.

432
01:04:10,930 --> 01:04:12,390
Get up. Get up.

433
01:04:21,770 --> 01:04:24,180
- No. No.- Wait! Wait!

434
01:04:24,270 --> 01:04:25,270
No!

435
01:05:09,810 --> 01:05:11,350
Fucking die!

436
01:06:44,930 --> 01:06:47,310
We need to fall back!

437
01:06:47,390 --> 01:06:50,270
Fall back behind the wall!

438
01:06:51,430 --> 01:06:53,020
- Fall back!- Fall back!

439
01:06:53,100 --> 01:06:54,600
Get out of the city!

440
01:06:56,100 --> 01:06:57,390
Fall back!

441
01:07:01,100 --> 01:07:02,470
Fall back!

442
01:07:02,560 --> 01:07:04,220
- Fall back!- Fall back!

443
01:09:00,390 --> 01:09:02,770
You can't stay here.

444
01:09:02,850 --> 01:09:04,470
You have to keep moving.

445
01:09:04,560 --> 01:09:06,140
We can't go out there.

446
01:09:06,220 --> 01:09:07,180
You have to.

447
01:09:08,430 --> 01:09:10,270
Everyone out there is dead.

448
01:09:11,560 --> 01:09:13,720
If you stay here, you'll die.

449
01:09:15,350 --> 01:09:16,350
Follow me.

450
01:09:18,220 --> 01:09:19,270
Follow me!

451
01:09:22,810 --> 01:09:24,560
Come on, quickly. Come to me.

452
01:09:24,640 --> 01:09:26,430
Lean him up there.

453
01:09:26,520 --> 01:09:28,430
Come on, quickly. All of you!

454
01:09:32,430 --> 01:09:33,430
Run!

455
01:09:39,270 --> 01:09:40,220
Run!

456
01:09:45,100 --> 01:09:47,100
Mama!

457
01:09:47,180 --> 01:09:48,470
Mama!

458
01:09:48,560 --> 01:09:50,520
Mama! No.

459
01:09:50,600 --> 01:09:52,470
Mama! Mama!

460
01:09:53,810 --> 01:09:54,770
Mama!

461
01:09:59,600 --> 01:10:01,390
Get up.

462
01:10:01,470 --> 01:10:02,890
Get up!

463
01:10:06,810 --> 01:10:08,020
We have to keep moving.

464
01:10:09,560 --> 01:10:11,060
Take her.

465
01:10:11,140 --> 01:10:13,020
Take her!

466
01:10:13,100 --> 01:10:15,600
- Take her.- Come on!

467
01:10:15,680 --> 01:10:16,640
Come on!

468
01:10:37,310 --> 01:10:38,310
This way.

469
01:11:28,680 --> 01:11:31,180
I want our baby to live.

470
01:11:34,020 --> 01:11:36,390
I want our baby to live.

471
01:11:38,970 --> 01:11:40,720
I want our baby to live.

472
01:11:42,390 --> 01:11:44,930
Don't let me die, Jaime.Please don't let me die.

473
01:11:45,020 --> 01:11:46,140
It's all right.

474
01:11:46,220 --> 01:11:48,140
- Please don't let me die.- It's all right.

475
01:11:48,150 --> 01:11:49,380
I don't want to die.

476
01:11:51,890 --> 01:11:53,640
Just look-- Look at me.

477
01:11:53,720 --> 01:11:56,170
- Look at me.- Not like this.

478
01:11:56,170 --> 01:11:57,750
Not like this. Not like this.

479
01:11:57,750 --> 01:11:59,140
Look-- Look-- Look me in the eye.

480
01:11:59,220 --> 01:12:00,790
Don't look away. Don't look--

481
01:12:00,800 --> 01:12:03,370
Look at me! Just look at me.

482
01:12:07,560 --> 01:12:09,770
Nothing else matters.

483
01:12:12,310 --> 01:12:14,350
Nothing else matters.

484
01:12:14,430 --> 01:12:16,310
Only us.

